    schema:datePosted "2026-09-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About Gladia Gladia builds the audio AI infrastructure behind the new generation of voice products. Our mission is to give every voice platform true conversational intelligence — the audio infrastructure that understands every conversation, turning voice into the world's most valuable data layer. Our API turns real-world conversational audio into accurate, structured, real-time output — powered by our proprietary Solaria ASR, across 100+ languages, with industry-leading latency. Hundreds of companies build their voice products on Gladia — from meeting assistants and voice agents to sales-enablement and contact-center platforms. We started in Paris, our growth is developer-led and heavily US-driven (and we're going after the US market hard). Headquartered in vibrant tech hubs like Paris and New York City, Gladia has been by OVH Groupe — Europe's leading cloud provider — and now operates as a fully autonomous brand and company within the Group. We're guided by four values: Honest — Say the real thing, kindly. Smart — Work smart, ship fast. Builders — Own your scope, build to last. Caring — Support people, take pride in the craft. About the role Gladia's web experience is evolving toward something richer — more immersive, interactive, and product-grade — and that evolution sits at the center of this role. This is a hybrid craft: you design and you build in code, across both our external surface and our internal products. That means three things: Our external product — the marketing site and materials — where we're pushing toward more immersive and interactive experiences. Our internal platform and brand system — the code-native, AI-powered system that generates all our assets — which you'll own and grow as a product in its own right. Our products — Compare STT, GladiaFlow, and our developer experience platform — which you'll design and help build. AI is at the core of our product, and increasingly at the core of how we design: our brand runs on a custom system that's prompt-driven and code-native. Strong web skills are non-negotiable — our website is hand-coded (Next.js, HTML, CSS) in Cursor and hosted on Vercel, so comfort with Cursor or an equivalent IDE is a prerequisite, alongside real fluency and curiosity around AI tools. You work with a high degree of autonomy: you anticipate needs, reach out directly to the teams you support without waiting to be briefed, are comfortable managing external partners when needed, and you're used to moving fast. What you'll do Lead the evolution of our web experience toward immersive, interactive, product-grade design across our marketing site and materials Design and build directly in code (Next.js, HTML, CSS), working in an IDE like Cursor and shipping through GitHub, deployed on Vercel Own and evolve our internal platform and AI-powered brand system — the product that generates all our assets — using prompting as a core creative tool alongside traditional design craft Design and help build our smaller products: Compare STT, GladiaFlow, and our developer experience platform Own Gladia's brand identity end-to-end across our website, marketing materials, decks, and video Move fast and deliver independently across a wide range of formats What we're looking for Visual design and design-engineering experience — you design and you code — ideally at a startup, having owned surfaces end-to-end rather than executed against an existing brief Fluency with front-end (React/Next.js, HTML, CSS), confident enough to review and ship changes via GitHub, working in Cursor or an equivalent IDE Strong interaction and motion sensibility, with the ability to push a web experience toward richer, more immersive and interactive design Systems thinking: you've built or operated a design system as a living product, not a static style guide A real, hands-on relationship with AI tools in your workflow — genuine daily use, not occasional dabbling The ability to build a distinct visual language for a technical, abstract product, without leaning on stock photography or literal product screenshots Sharp, fast decision-making, with the ability to clearly explain the reasoning behind your choices Fluent English Based in or open to working on-site in Paris, as a big plus Compensation & benefits €65,000–€85,000 base salary, depending on experience Hybrid work from our Paris office or full-remote in France ~€200/month lunch vouchers €360/year sports allowance €300 workstation adaptation budget Full health coverage Pension benefits Flexible vacation policy Please submit your application in English. It’s our company language so you’ll be speaking lots of it if you join. We treat all candidates equally - if you’re interested please apply through our careers portal. Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow" ;
