    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "remote-devops-engineer-cimar-london-437460" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-14"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Company Overview CIMAR UK Ltd, now a part of DeepHealth, is a leading provider in the SaaS (Software-as-a-Service) healthcare sector, specialising in advanced cloud-based image management solutions. Our technology empowers healthcare organisations to optimise image management processes, enhance patient care, and streamline workflows through seamless integration and actionable data insights. Job Summary The DevOps Engineer is a hands-on engineering role within the Platform Engineering team, responsible for supporting and evolving DeepHealth's AWS-based infrastructure, Kubernetes platforms, CI/CD tooling, and operational processes. Working closely with the Senior Platform Engineer, this role focuses on infrastructure automation, cloud operations, platform reliability, and continuous improvement. The DevOps Engineer plays an important part in helping development teams deliver software efficiently while ensuring that DeepHealth's infrastructure remains secure, scalable, and resilient. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Design, build, and maintain AWS cloud infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code tooling (Terraform or equivalent), ensuring consistency, repeatability, and version control. · Manage and improve Kubernetes platforms (EKS or similar), including cluster configuration, scaling, upgrades, and reliability. · Build, maintain, and improve CI/CD pipelines to support fast, reliable software delivery across development teams. · Monitor platform health and performance, respond to incidents, and drive root cause analysis and resolution to maintain high availability. · Automate operational processes and repetitive tasks to reduce toil and improve team efficiency. · Implement and maintain cloud security best practices including IAM policies, network security, secrets management, and vulnerability scanning. · Support development teams with platform tooling, onboarding to infrastructure services, and resolving environment-level issues. · Manage container image pipelines and registry, including security scanning and lifecycle management. · Maintain clear and up-to-date documentation of infrastructure, processes, runbooks, and architectural decisions. · Contribute to cost monitoring and optimisation across cloud services, identifying inefficiencies and recommending improvements. PLEASE NOTE: This is not an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities and requirements of the position described above. Other functions may be assigned and management retains the right to add or change duties at any time. Minimum Qualifications, Education and Experience: · Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience (required). · 5+ years of experience in a DevOps, platform engineering, or cloud infrastructure role (required). · Hands-on experience with AWS cloud services (EC2, EKS, RDS, S3, IAM, VPC, and related) (required). · Experience managing Kubernetes clusters in production environments (required). · Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines using tools such as GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Jenkins, or equivalent (required). · Proficiency with Infrastructure as Code, preferably Terraform (required). · Scripting skills in Python, Bash, or similar for automation (required). · Solid understanding of networking fundamentals including DNS, load balancing, firewalls, and VPNs (required). · Security-conscious approach to infrastructure design and operations (required). · Preferred: Experience with observability and monitoring tooling (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, or similar). · Preferred: Familiarity with GitOps practices and tooling (e.g., ArgoCD, Flux). · Preferred: AWS certification (e.g., AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, AWS Solutions Architect). · Preferred: Experience in a regulated industry such as healthcare or finance. Quality Standards • Communicates, cooperates, and consistently functions professionally and harmoniously with all levels of supervision, co-workers, visitors, and vendors. • Demonstrates initiative, personal awareness, professionalism and integrity, and exercises confidentiality in all areas of performance. • Follows all local, regional and country laws concerning employment. • Follows all DeepHealth policies and procedures. • Follows data privacy, compliance, safety and confidentiality standards at all times. • Practices universal safety precautions. • Promotes good public relations on the phone and in person. • Adapts and is willing to learn new tasks, methods, and systems. • Reports to work regularly as scheduled; consistently punctual with respect to working hours, meal and rest breaks, and maintains satisfactory personal attendance in accordance with DeepHealth guidelines. • Completes job responsibilities in a quality and timely manner. Physical Demands This position often requires sitting, standing, walking, bending, twisting, reaching with hands and arms, using hands and fingers, handling, or feeling, speaking, listening, and high-level cognitive thinking. Also, must be able to lift up to 10 pounds occasionally. Travel This position may require occasional travel. Working Environment Remote “The employee must be able to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Salary £60,000 - £70,000 per year Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
