    schema:datePosted "2026-09-14"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Your Mission: Join the Pinnacle of Satellite Technology Advancement in Germany! Reflex Aerospace is at the forefront of propelling high-performance satellite technology to new heights within the German aerospace landscape. As part of Reflex Aerospace, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the trajectory of the space industry's future. This is an opportunity to contribute your expertise and enthusiasm to a team that stands for innovation and excellence. As Software Engineer - Systems Modeling you will join the Architecture and Processes (A&P) team to develop the system infrastructure that enables the rapid development of satellite missions. You will work closely with all engineering teams to develop tools, digital models, and processes to enable our mission teams. Your Background: You hold a university degree in Computer Science, Aerospace Engineering or a related field, or bring equivalent work experience. You have experience with MBSE, SysMLv2, and code-based systems modeling. You have strong Python skills and are experienced in architecture, testing, automation, databases, and API interfacing. You are proficient with Git, GitLab, and CI pipelines - you should be comfortable managing branches, handling merge requests, and troubleshooting CI issues independently. You are structured and process-oriented with a keen sense of simplicity and automation. You are a collaborative team player and communicate effortlessly with different stakeholders. Ideally, you already bring an understanding of satellite missions, system architectures, satellite subsystems and the satellite development lifecycle. Ideally, you have experience with UI design for data visualization, databases (PostgreSQL, InfluxDB), and Grafana. What We Offer: Collaborate with a diverse multinational team crafting the next wave of cutting-edge satellites. Embark on this exciting journey with us from the outset, leaving your indelible mark on a dynamic company and playing a direct role in shaping the future of the space industry. Keep your energy levels high with company-sponsored memberships for Urban Sports Club as well a discount in the public transport. Access to Corporate Benefits - a website with many discounts for various brands. An annual training budget of 1.500€. We exclusively offer permanent employment contracts, reflecting our commitment to building long-term relationships and supporting sustainable career growth within our organization. A 20% contribution to your private pension plan. We provide a hybrid work model along with flexible working hours, empowering you as the owner of your time management. Enjoy 30 days of paid vacation and a special company holiday on April 12th, celebrating the International Day of Human Space Flight and the spirit of exploration. Join Reflex Aerospace and be a driving force in shaping the next era of space exploration! We look forward to your application. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
