    schema:datePosted "2026-09-14"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "At Instagrid, you are part of the clean-tech revolution by bringing pure energy into your region, helping professional workers transitioning away from combustion generators and making it possible for them to experience a safe, efficient, clean and silent energy solution. Your Mission Instagrid is scaling fast — and our procurement function needs to keep pace, not just strategically, but operationally. As a Working Student in Direct Procurement, you're at the center of daily execution: securing component availability, managing supplier interactions, running RFQs, and making sure our contract manufacturers always have what they need to build. You'll work in a supportive setup, but with genuine exposure to how a lean procurement team operates in a fabless environment. You'll report into our Procurement team and collaborate closely with Strategic and Operational Sourcing, with involvement in new product introductions and supply chain activities. The scope spans electromechanical components, battery-related materials, and full product assemblies — across engineering samples, NPI, and series production. Your Impact Own daily operational purchasing: order management, delivery tracking, and availability monitoring for direct materials across our supply network Run RFQs end-to-end — from initial inquiry and cost comparison through sample orders to series supply handover Support early engineering phases with price indications and supplier benchmarks, anchoring cost targets before designs are locked Act as the operational point of contact for our contract manufacturers — tracking commitments, escalating deviations, and keeping supply on track Maintain and continuously improve purchasing data quality in NetSuite: lead times, MOQs, pricing, and supplier records Contribute to cost-down initiatives through BoM-level price benchmarking and cross-supplier comparisons Play an active role in building leaner, more digital purchasing processes through AI applications and automation Currently enrolled in a degree program in economics, business administration, engineering, or a comparable field First practical experience in procurement, supply chain, or operations — internships count Comfortable with electromechanical components, assemblies, or hardware products: you understand what you're buying Structured and reliable: you track your own tasks, follow up without reminders, and flag issues before they escalate Clear and direct in supplier communication — confident in writing and conversation, in both German and English Fluent in German and English; both are required for daily business Nice to have: experience with NetSuite or a comparable ERP system; background in electronics, battery systems, or EMS and contract manufacturing environments Your Benefits Real responsibility from day one — not busywork, but meaningful ownership of live procurement tasks Full-cycle exposure: from engineering support and RFQ through negotiation to series supply A lean, senior team that gives direct feedback and expects you to push back when something doesn't add up An inside view of what it takes to scale a hardware company — across supply chain, operations, and beyond Flexible working hours coordinated around your university schedule Generous holiday entitlement plus additional special leave days, on a pro-rata basis This is Instagrid Pure instant power. Anywhere. We have created the world’s most advanced portable power supplies, bringing freedom to the way our customers work. With you we want to shape a world where advanced technology meets environmental responsibility and create lasting impact. Driven by our curiosity and the desire to leave tomorrow's world cleaner than we found it yesterday. Join us in transitioning away from combustion generators to a cleaner alternative for fast, measurable, and real outcomes. What we’ve achieved so far is just the beginning. At Instagrid, we are deeply committed to equal employment opportunities as we believe in the power of diverse teams. We do not just accept diversity but actively search for the best talent regardless of gender, ethnic origin, age, religion, sexual orientation or place of origin. Working as a team, we treat each other with respect and value each other’s opinions to achieve our common goals. We are looking forward to receiving your application! Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
